-- TRIEL example inside the formal core: a physical system with a sensor. The
-- drive motor of an industrial robot arm overheats, and the specification
-- states what its work cell, the arm with the controller that drives it, must
-- do about it.
--
-- One activation of the specification is one incident: the activation entry
-- is the moment the overheat alarm is raised, and every duration counts from
-- it (formal/core/CORE.md, section 8.3, point 5), as in
-- gdpr_art33_notification.triel. The controller must stop the drive within 30
-- seconds of the alarm; a stop exactly at the deadline fulfils the obligation.
-- A missed deadline is a breach, which stays on record, and the obligation is
-- escalated: the safety engineer must then stop the drive within 30 seconds of
-- the breach, a stop exactly at the breach not included (formal/core/CORE.md,
-- section 8.3, point 10). The arm must not move when the motor temperature is
-- at or above the limit; the condition is read in the state of the entry just
-- before each movement. The temperature should come back below the limit
-- within 10 minutes of the alarm.
--
-- The temperature is quoted by a sensor, an ORACLE, so PROVENANCE_REQUIRED is
-- true (TECHNICAL_REPORT.md section 2.9). A reading is fresh for 5 seconds
-- after it arrives, an age of exactly 5 seconds included (MAX_AGE 5 SECONDS
-- ON_STALE BLOCK, fresh_at_max_age); a reading that is older, or present at
-- activation without an arrival, is absent (stale_absent; examples/core/
-- README.md, conventions 3 and 4). So when the sensor is silent, or its data
-- are stale, the temperature is absent and:
--
-- - the condition of the prohibition is undefined. The verdict of the
--   prohibition records a breach only when its condition is true, so it stays
--   PENDING; the fail-closed monitor of the prohibition blocks the movement,
--   since the condition is not known to be false (MONITOR ... BLOCK;
--   undefined_guard_blocks_not_breach);
-- - the invariant is undefined (U): missing data neither fulfil nor violate
--   EVENTUALLY ... WITHIN (convention 11).
--
-- No reading is fresh at the activation entry, since its event is the
-- activation and not an arrival, and that entry is inside the 10 minutes. So
-- in this specification the invariant is never F: it is T once a fresh reading
-- below the limit arrives in time, and U otherwise. F would say that the
-- temperature was known to be at or above the limit at every entry up to the
-- deadline, the alarm included; at the alarm no fresh reading says so
-- (ew_undefined_data, cmp_undefined).
--
-- Only the monitor of the prohibition blocks a movement; the invariant
-- reports, it does not block.
--
-- Limit of the core: every duration counts from the activation, and a
-- condition has no access to time, so a condition "at or above the limit for
-- longer than N seconds", counted from an arbitrary moment of the trace, is not
-- computed inside the core. A deadline inside a branch of IF or WHEN, which
-- would count from the moment the branch is taken, is rejected by the
-- translator (formal/core/CORE.md, section 10.6, further rejections); the
-- condition of IF or WHEN is read once, in the first state of the trace
-- (convention 6); and ON ... DO, which waits for an event, is outside the core.
-- The example therefore counts from the activation by the alarm. The duration
-- can instead be quoted: a factor such as seconds_over_limit, sent by the
-- sensor under ON_STALE BLOCK, with arm MUST_NOT move WHEN seconds_over_limit
-- > 30, is inside the core, and the specification then trusts the sensor's
-- count. Conditions compare values and do not compute them: the sensor quotes
-- the temperature, and the specification does not model the motor. Every
-- construct in this file is translated into the Isabelle/HOL core
-- (formal/core) and evaluated by the exported evaluator (evaluator/).

SPECIFICATION sensor_overheat VERSION 1.0.0
    PROVENANCE_REQUIRED: true

SUBJECTS {
  controller      : SYSTEM,
  arm             : SYSTEM,
  temp_sensor     : ORACLE,
  safety_engineer : PARTY
}

TERMS {
  controller MUST stop_drive WITHIN 30 SECONDS;
  controller ON_BREACH ESCALATE_TO safety_engineer;
  arm MUST_NOT move WHEN motor_temp >= limit_c
}

FACTORS {
  motor_temp : Decimal METADATA SOURCE temp_sensor MAX_AGE 5 SECONDS ON_STALE BLOCK,
  limit_c    : Decimal METADATA
}

INVARIANTS {
  cooled_down : LIVENESS : EVENTUALLY(motor_temp < limit_c) WITHIN 10 MINUTES
}
